  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving Unconditional Cash Assistance to Drought-Affected Households in Burhakaba District, Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe proposed project aims to improve food access for 1703&#xa0;severely food-insecure households in five villages (Afar Abawle, Arey Wiin, Awyaaye Donki, Masuusow and Warfi) of&#xa0;Burhakaba District who have been affected by recurrent flooding and climatic shocks. The project will focus on providing life-saving, short-term support to households facing IPC Phase 3 (Crisis) and at risk of IPC Phase 4 (Emergency) food insecurity, with particular attention to the most vulnerable groups, including female-headed households, households with persons with disabilities, child-headed households, minority clan households, and households with malnourished women and children.&#xa0;The project will implement community mobilization and beneficiary verification to ensure transparent, inclusive, and needs-based targeting. This will be followed by the provision of unconditional cash transfers for three months to enable targeted households to meet their immediate food and basic needs in a dignified manner. By improving household purchasing power in a context of functioning local markets, the project will help stabilize food consumption, reduce reliance on negative coping strategies, and prevent further deterioration of food security conditions during the lean period.&#xa0;The project&apos;s target villages will include Afar Abawle, Arey Wiin, Awyaaye Donki, Masuusow and Warfi.&#xa0;lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
